Nathan Russell wrote:
> At which probability do wizards get "This spellbook is very difficult
> to comprehend. Continue?"  I never ignore that message (I sometimes
> read a merely difficult book in controlled conditions - DL 1, level
> cleared, etc).

The code from 3.4.3 reads:
If the spellbook is blessed or the Book of the Dead,
you always succeed in reading it (though reading the Book of the
Dead results in reciting rather than learning a spell).

Otherwise, if the spellbook is cursed, it is always too hard
to read.

Otherwise, your reading ability is based on your current
intelligence, level, the spellbook's level, and whether you're
wearing lenses.  If you have less than 100% chance of successfully
reading the book as a wizard and not confused, you are warned.
You are never warned when confused.  If your chance is less
than 3/5, the spellbook is "very difficult."  Otherwise, it
is only "difficult."

